              "answer": "process_delivery checks receipts before send_request, acknowledges 2xx, and delegates other statuses to schedule_retry. retry_allowed permits 429 or 5xx while attempt < 3. schedule_retry copies the job and changes only attempt, preserving delivery_id. send_request sends that identifier as Idempotency-Key. delivery_key derives the initial identifier from event and endpoint. ReceiptStore keeps acknowledgements in memory: protection is lost on restart or pruning; check/send/mark is not atomic, so concurrent workers can still send twice. The receiver must implement idempotency; the header alone does not prove it. Transport exceptions are not converted into retryable status codes. Offline scripted contract fixture; not a model-quality result."
